      "application": "Application & ProcessThe  Passion's  Tippler-Lifting or Tipping Device is a hydraulic device that uses an arm for lifting and turning an FBD bowl by 180 degrees. It is used to unload material from a fluid bed dryer bowl into a Cone Mill, Multi Mill or Oscillating Granulator in a dust-free manner for downsizing or dry milling and collected in IBC Bin. The operation is completely dust-free and eliminates manual handling or scooping. To use the device, the FBD bowl is placed beneath the tipper and the inverted cone of the tipper is lowered until the brim flange of the bowl touches the inverted cone. Both components are then clamped together using quick-fixing clamps and the entire assembly is raised and tilting.",
